<h2>Questions about why concert tickets are so expensive</h2>
<details class="so-faq"><summary>Why are concert tickets so expensive compared with years ago?</summary><p>Prices depend on demand, seat location, event popularity and availability, plus fees. Popular tours with few dates tend to cost the most.</p></details>
<details class="so-faq"><summary>Who sets the face value of a ticket?</summary><p>Event organizers, performers or promoters determine ticket pricing.</p></details>
<details class="so-faq"><summary>Are resale tickets always more expensive?</summary><p>No. Sellers set resale prices, so they can be above or below face value.</p></details>
<details class="so-faq"><summary>What are service fees for?</summary><p>They help cover payment processing, support, platform upkeep and security.</p></details>
<details class="so-faq"><summary>Where can I find a better price?</summary><p>Compare sections, check totals, and watch <a href="/ticket-deals">ticket deals</a>. No marketplace can promise the lowest price for every event.</p></details>
